  "description": "Reid Blacktop 1.0 ST | 500W commuter eBike\nPowerful 500W electric assistance and easy step-through access – the Reid Blacktop 1.0 ST is designed to make everyday urban journeys more convenient and comfortable, with speeds of up to 32km/h.\nThe Reid Blacktop 1.0 ST is built for riders looking for a practical, powerful and accessible way to get around town. Its step-through frame makes getting on and off easier, while the upgraded 500W, 48V motor delivers electric assistance for commuting, running errands and everyday urban travel. With speeds of up to 32km/h, it offers a convenient way to cover city distances with less effort.\nA larger 13.4Ah battery supports your daily journeys, while the throttle provides an additional way to access motor power. An LCD display keeps essential ride information within easy reach, helping you stay informed while on the move.\nEquipped with practical commuter accessories as standard, the Blacktop 1.0 ST includes mudguards, a rear rack and a heavy-duty rear stand, making it ready for everyday use. Ergonomic grips add comfort, while Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with a motor cut-off feature help maintain control by interrupting motor assistance when braking.\nCombining a step-through design with powerful electric assistance and useful everyday features, the Blacktop 1.0 ST is designed to make urban travel simpler and more flexible.\nThe Blacktop 1.0 ST is ideal for:\n\nEasy everyday access, with a step-through frame that makes mounting and dismounting more convenient\n\nRiders seeking powerful electric assistance, with an upgraded 500W, 48V motor\n\nUrban commuting, with assistance reaching speeds of up to 32km/h\n\nRiders wanting flexible power delivery, with a throttle alongside electric assistance\n\nDaily journeys, supported by a larger 13.4Ah battery\n\nPractical commuting, with mudguards, a rear rack and a heavy-duty rear stand included as standard\n\nComfort-focused urban riding, with ergonomic grips and an LCD display\n\nControlled braking, with Tektro brakes featuring a motor cut-off function\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
